de rebel teen  energy something that i vastly prefer  over the more whimsical and cartoony  designs of most shonen before this era  there's also the sheikai and bankai that  came in all shades of cool thanks to the  brilliance of daite gubo ghostbusters  turned into dragon ball z with magical  sword samurais and battles against gods  how epic can you be easily anime of the  year 2005.  for me 2005's were the transition to the  next era of anime started while the  anime sphere was quite heavy on sci-fi  the midpoint of the decades where things  started transitioning to softer sci-fi  instead of robots and steampunk settings  we now begin to see more anime taking  place in the modern neighborhood filled  with supernatural elements lore of yueki  comes to mind and i hope that more  people will share their fond memories of  this one then a perennial favorite of  mine with the urban fantasy setting is  shakugan no shana i do have a strong  bias for it but i came really close to  crowning it this year ultimately it  stands as a runner-up side by side with  my personal pick for this year blood  plus way before the vampire craze blood  plus gave us a glimpse of it as it  combines horror and action that while  may not seem too original in terms of  premise ended up being an awesome ride  it's an action show that carefully  trends the line between pg-13 and r18  and as teenagers nothing can be cooler  for us back in the day than that right  overall blood plus is probably one of  the more generally good shows that i can  recommend to people thanks to its high  octane action and sleek art and  animation plus not a lot of fan service  or cliches often associated with anime  these days and that's speaking in a  relative manner still the high fantasy  and medievalist settings aren't dead  with that basilisk subasa chronicle and  trinity blood for those who wanted some  hot blooded sports action 2005 also gave  us eye shield 21  2006.  2006  is  a  banger there's no other way to put it so  let's get on with this amazing year as  said in the series clause standout  sequels will be given shout outs so  here's to helsing ultimate thanks for  your help in making 2006 awesome good  friend dean stay night it also made its  debut in 2006 and we at the time had no  idea what the fate series would end up  turning into the following decade it  shows that some of the most hyped anime  movie trilogies and video game cash cows  all had to start from humble beginnings  ray kugimiya continues to roll in  cementing her status as the 2000 sunday  queen with a familiar of zero it's  around this time that the sharna clones  have started coming around and gogimiya  herself would continue getting  star-making roles the next few years in  non-action anime mind you shonen shows  continue trying to make their mark with  varied levels of success while d greyman  is now more known for the manga going on  hiatus it was a big deal back then the  latte can be said of hitman reborn  although that manga had the benefit of  ending conclusively to a mixed reception  2006 though came down to two mega hits  that shaped the anime landscape on one  hand you have code geass hailed by many  as one of the greatest anime ever made  it's not hard to argue with the facts  it's such a cultural landmark that  continues to get new movies and series  made and it really made such a big  impact with its masterful mixing of  genres you get the mecca the  psychological the political peppered by  the handsome guys and waifus it would  have been a no-brainer to give code  ghias the crown but it unfortunately ran  into another powerhouse series of 2006  gintama gintama also does the genre  mixing well comedy action drama i mean  need i say more it goes all out in  parodies and gives you fits of laughter  before slamming you with some of the  most epic sword fights and brawls that  you've ever seen in anime then it hits  you hard with touching backstories that  will stick with you for years to co