 call it emblematic  of what you'd expect of these hidden gem  anime of this era but it's one of those  shows that you can take one look at and  immediately get a flashback of a bygone  era in anime's history it's also got a  dub with a stellar reputation so you  might want to check that out too  2008  as we approach the end of the decade we  start seeing those big hitters not to  say that these shows are any less good  but it's just that the action series  around this time never reached the  influence the previous big hit has had  off the top of my head the most popular  amongst the 2008 badge is possibly a  certain magical index yet another urban  fantasy that i love look i just love  these urban fantasies with supernatural  elements and pseudo-harems if it's not  obvious by now in its time index was  wildly popular and spawn numerous  spin-offs while it's a shell of itself  now in terms of popularity the a certain  series of anime still ends up making a  bit of noise when new titles get  announced i think more people like  railgun a lot better though 2008 also  had black butler probably on par with  index in terms of popularity the first  season i mean i really loved it the  second season  not so much but it's still a landmark  show that got a lot of female fans into  the whole anime thing it's not just for  the girls though remember and i'll vouch  for the interesting developments and  plot that the first season gave us start  for the premise and the banger opening  by sid stay for the suspenseful plot and  the action ultimately the win goes to  soul eater while the previous two titles  of their niches an index in particular  has a universe that's a can of worms  which isn't quite different from the  fate series solita's a more accessible  show to get into it's an entertaining  supernatural action show that has a  little of everything and could help a  prospective viewer ease into an anime  watching habit while lacking the  gratuitous levels of fan service that  the creators otherworld fire force had  gotten flak for other niche hits in this  era include birdie the mighty and real  drive if the synopsis interest you you  should definitely check those ones out  2009  now i find myself in a bit of a bind  remember the series clause it prevents  me from outright crowning what many  consider to be one of the best anime of  all time yes the king of my anime list  everyone's favorite fma brotherhood the  title is well deserved too personally i  think perfection is something that is  statistically impossible but fma  brotherhood just has so many things  going for it whether you like it for the  plot the character stories the drama the  art the themes and meaning or just all  of it fmab has something that would  strike deep and embed itself into your  heart for years to come heck i throw the  show into contention for anime of the  decade and i'm confident that it would  definitely get the win that's just how  good it is with the consensus action  anime of the year out of the running  what are we left with then well phantom  eden of the east sengoku basala canaan  oh fairy tale also got its start this  year so let's go with that one it's not  a debate that among those i mentioned  fairy tale is by far the show that gets  the mainstream appeal a light-hearted  adventure show that takes us through the  sights and sound of hiro mashima's  colorful world managed to garner quite a  lot of love from anime fans you can say  what you want about the latter part of  fairy tale and the memes about nakama  power fake deaths and fanservice but the  magic was literally there in the first  few arcs that part of the show really  displayed mashima's pedigree in writing  light adventures and serious plots along  with creating characters that you all  grow to love and care about  2010  we've reached the end point of the video  so what does the anime world look like  well some show called chaon was raising  eyebrows left and right and ushering a  new 